config BR2_PACKAGE_THINGINO_ISP_GUARD
	bool "Boot guard for the open ISP stack"
	default n
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_THINGINO_ISP_OPEN
	help
	  Install /etc/init.d/S10isp-guard, a crash-loop guard for the
	  open-tx-isp kernel modules: a boot that does not stay up for 300 s
	  with timpsd running makes the next boot skip the ISP and sensor
	  modules and timps (the camera stays reachable over SSH and the
	  web UI; "S10isp-guard clear" re-arms it). The u-boot variable
	  isp_open=auto|manual|off selects the behaviour.

	  Meant for development and bring-up of the open stack. Do not
	  enable it on cameras that must keep streaming through repeated
	  power loss: two reboots within five minutes leave the streamer
	  off until someone clears the guard.
